cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the code or the records in this repository, please cite them
  using the metadata below. The manuscript "Estimand Drift under Spatial Block
  Hold-Out" is under review at MDPI Mathematics; once it is published, please
  cite the article as well.
title: "Estimand Drift under Spatial Block Hold-Out: reproducibility package"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package of the manuscript "Estimand Drift under Spatial
  Block Hold-Out" by L. F. C. Seelig and R. M. Salles (submitted to MDPI
  Mathematics, under review). It holds the code that partitions and trims
  sixteen simulated city x quadrant cells at block sizes of 10 km and 5 km,
  the computation of the per-node inclusion probabilities, the split draws,
  the numerical tests, the training and evaluation code of a graph neural
  network and a graph-free multilayer perceptron, the per-run records of the
  trained models, the aggregation scripts, and the tables and figures of the
  article. The large data files are listed with size and SHA-256 in
  manifest/data_manifest.csv and are available from the corresponding author
  on request.
type: software
authors:
